      "writtenOn": "2024-10-26T03:19:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To test this on an existing lineage install:\n\n  1. adb root\n  2. adb push apns-conf.xml /data/misc/apns/apns-conf.xml\n  3. adb shell \"sed -i -E \u0027s/(\u003cstring name\u003d.ro_build_id.\u003e)[^\u003c]+(\u003c.string\u003e)/\\1dummy\\2/g\u0027 /data/user_de/0/com.android.providers.telephony/shared_prefs/build-id.xml\"\n  4. adb reboot\n  5. reset apn settings via the three-dot menu in the apn list\n  6. reset network settings via the button in the internet settings toolbar\n  7. adb reboot\n\nThis will persist even through OTA updates since it takes precedence\nover the shipped /product/etc/apns-conf.xml.\n\nTo undo it, do the same thing, but delete /data/misc/apns/apns-conf.xml\nin step 2.",
      "revId": "ab752bf599dad939f80f5e9e14023845e37b0980",
      "serverId": "1ec6b3db-b2c1-4fa4-84a2-4c7efe89ba71"
    },
